  "prompts": {
    "organize": "You organise a parent's notes about their child, {name}, into passport entries that help other carers understand {name}.\nRules:\n- Use ONLY facts stated in the NOTES. Never add advice, guesses or facts of your own.\n- Make one entry per distinct fact.\n- section is one of: communication, calming, upsets, likes, pain, medical, routine, safety.\n- signal: what a carer sees or hears, or the fact itself. At most 15 words.\n- meaning: what it means. Fill it for communication and pain entries; otherwise use an empty string.\n- whatToDo: what helps, only if the NOTES say so; otherwise an empty string.\n- quote: copy 3 to 12 words EXACTLY, word for word, from the NOTES that support the entry.\n\nNOTES:\n\"\"\"\n{notes}\n\"\"\"",
    "answer": "You help a carer look after {name}, a child who cannot easily explain themselves.\nThe carer says: \"{question}\"\n\nThese are the ONLY facts you may use, from {name}'s passport, written by the parent:\n{facts}\n\nRules:\n- Use only these facts. Never add medical advice or anything not in them.\n- answer: at most 3 short, calm sentences (under 60 words) saying what it probably means and what the carer should do. Talk to the carer directly as \"you\". The parent is {parent}: if the carer should contact the parent, say \"call {parent}\", never \"call me\". Do not write ids in the answer.\n- usedIds: the ids of the facts you used, for example [\"e2\"].\n- found: \"found\" if the facts clearly answer it, \"partial\" if they only help a little, \"none\" if none of them fit (then answer is an empty string).",
    "observation": "A carer noticed something new about {name}: \"{observation}\"\n\nCurrent passport entries that may be related:\n{facts}\n\nPropose ONE passport change using only what the carer said.\n- action: \"add\" for a new fact, or \"edit\" to improve an existing entry (then set editId to its id).\n- section is one of: communication, calming, upsets, likes, pain, medical, routine, safety.\n- signal, meaning and whatToDo follow the same meaning as the existing entries. Use empty strings for parts the carer did not say."
  }
